virglrenderer: Venus ends an app's context before Metal ends QEMU on too many passes

What: vkr counts the Metal passes (render encoders) each command buffer opens: a clear of
an image (one per level of its ranges; the layers of a level are one layered pass), a
render pass begin and each next subpass, a dynamic rendering begin, a blit or resolve
region, on KosmicKrisp a barrier inside a pass (it splits a multisampled pass there; vkr
does not keep the pass's samples, so every in-pass barrier counts there), and the
secondaries a primary executes (their passes each time). A command buffer may open
16384 (OMACVM_VENUS_ENCODER_CAP, tests only); a MoltenVK batch (all command buffers of
one VkSubmitInfo or VkSubmitInfo2) twice that. The command past it is refused before the
driver gets it, and the app's context ends with a log line (the guest recorded and
submitted without waiting: it sees a lost device). Draws, copies, fills, updates and
attachment clears do not count.
Why: Metal ends the process (SIGABRT: "Failed to allocate IOGPUDeviceShmem" in
IOGPUMetalCommandBufferStorageGrowKernelCommandBuffer, from AGX::RenderContext::
beginRenderPass) when one Metal command buffer has about 98304 passes. One guest program
ended QEMU and the VM so, with no submit on KosmicKrisp: probes through vkr's dispatch
on the M1 Max (macOS 27, the 3.2.18 drivers, work/v624-hostmem): KosmicKrisp aborted
while recording past 98304 clears of one level (run7-9; 90000 with 150000 asked), past
98304 empty passes (run10), between 90112 and 98304 in-pass barriers of a 4x pass and
between 6144 and 6656 clears of 15 levels; 1M
draws, 204800 copies, 204800 1x in-pass barriers and 200 clears of 2048 layers did not.
MoltenVK aborted at the encode: with prefill at vkEndCommandBuffer after 150000 clears,
204800 passes, renderings, blits or resolves; without prefill at vkQueueSubmit of one
batch of 8 x 16384 clears (4 x 16384 in one batch, 8 batches of 16384 and 8 submits
went through). KosmicKrisp took 8 x 16384 in one batch and 16 live command buffers of
16384 each (also over 2 contexts). 16384 is 6x below the abort; a Zink frame has about
2000 passes. The M4 and an 8 GB Mac are not measured yet (the cap stays fixed).
Upstream: OmacVM policy; nothing posted.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the h-pass- cases: the legal maximum and one
past it per kind at a cap of 1024, the default cap, 100000 clears that ended the process
before, levels, layers, secondaries, a real MoltenVK batch).

